        "problem": "Let $P={{y}_{0},{y}_{1},\u2026,{y}_{n}}$ be a partition of the interval $[1,5].$ If $\u0394{y}_{j}={y}_{j}-{y}_{j-1},$ calculate ${\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({y}_{j}+{y}_{j-1})\u0394{y}_{j}.$",
        "worked_solution": "We can simplify the given summation as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({y}_{j}+{y}_{j-1})\u0394{y}_{j} & =({y}_{1}+{y}_{0})\u0394{y}_{1}+({y}_{2}+{y}_{1})\u0394{y}_{2}+\u22ef+({y}_{n}+{y}_{n-1})\u0394{y}_{n} \\\\  & =({y}_{1}+{y}_{0})({y}_{1}-{y}_{0})+({y}_{2}+{y}_{1})({y}_{2}-{y}_{1})+\u22ef+({y}_{n}+{y}_{n-1})({y}_{n}-{y}_{n-1}) \\\\  & =({y}_{1}^{2}-{y}_{0}^{2})+({y}_{2}^{2}-{y}_{1}^{2})+\u22ef+({y}_{n}^{2}-{y}_{n-1}^{2}) \\\\  & =(\\cancel{{y}_{1}^{2}}-{y}_{0}^{2})+(\\cancel{{y}_{2}^{2}}-\\cancel{{y}_{1}^{2}})+\u22ef+({y}_{n}^{2}-\\cancel{{y}_{n-1}^{2}}) \\\\  & =-{y}_{0}^{2}+{y}_{n}^{2} \\\\  & ={y}_{n}^{2}-{y}_{0}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since ${y}_{0}=1$ and ${y}_{n}=5$ are the endpoints of our partition, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({y}_{j}+{y}_{j-1})\u0394{y}_{i} & ={y}_{n}^{2}-{y}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & ={5}^{2}-{1}^{2} \\\\  & =24.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
